    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d74">

                <pb facs="0085" n="75" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg75"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/947: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-11T19:00:00-05:00">December 11, 1941—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>566. Your 728, December 10, 10 p.m.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d74-f1"/> You may make
                    the following statement to the Minister of Foreign Affairs <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Government of the United States, as it has publicly stated,
                            considers that the defense of each one of the American Republics is <pb
                                facs="0086" n="76" xml:id="pg76"/> vital to the defense of all the
                            others. Accordingly, the Government of the United States will
                            immediately cooperate, to the best of its ability, in the defense of any
                            American Republic against which aggression is committed from outside the
                            Western Hemisphere.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d74-f1" n="31" xml:id="d74-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it urged that assurance be given Chile of United States support,
                    should Chile be attacked by Japan.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
